<title>SPAIN: Santander 96 net attributable up 13.53 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander 96 net attributable up 13.53 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996 results to end December</p>
<p>				    (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 85.60  vs 75.39</p>
<p> Net profit				 120.53  vs 101.87</p>
<p> Pretax profit			    163.19  vs 146.00</p>
<p> Net interest income		    395.07  vs 349.78</p>
<p> Ordinary income			  636.79  vs 542.47</p>
<p> Operating income			 181.70  vs 145.35</p>
<p> Interest income			 1,573.02 vs  1,379.48</p>
<p> Equity-accounted dividends	     17.08 vs	8.04</p>
<p> Interest expenses		    -1,195.03 vs -1,037.74</p>
<p> Fees and commissions		    162.70 vs    137.04</p>
<p> Financial/trading income		 79.02 vs     55.66</p>
<p> Other operating results		  -5.53 vs	4.37</p>
<p> Operating costs			  -400.40 vs   -354.84</p>
<p>    -personnel costs		    -265.78 vs   -237.13</p>
<p>    -general, administrative costs  -134.62 vs   -117.71</p>
<p> Depreciation				-49.17 vs    -46.65</p>
<p>Net earnings from equity-accounted</p>
<p>    holdings				  26.45 vs     13.36</p>
<p> Amortisation of goodwill		-20.16 vs    -15.55</p>
<p> Earnings on grp transactions	   37.76 vs     16.56</p>
<p> Net loan-loss provisions		-59.42 vs    -34.12</p>
<p> Writedown of investment securities  -497   vs  1,005.00</p>
<p> Net extraordinary gains/losses   -2,646.00 vs 19,401.00</p>
<p> Corporate income tax		    -42.66 vs    -44.13</p>
<p>Total assets		     19,676.37  vs 16,464.96</p>
<p>NOTE - Category of &quot;earnings on group transactions&quot; includes Santander's sale of 2.2 percent stake in U.S. financial group First Union.</p>
<p>&quot;Extraordinaries&quot; includes increase in funds for early retirement.</p>
<p>A rise of 12.08 percent in personnel costs reflects the increase in staff after acquisitions.</p>
</text>
